[t=007 webapp:dev_forum] post_reply sequence=3 source=agent params={} status=200 post_id=p002 post_title=VSCode TS server can't find react types after restart — how do you reset it? author=tamsin body=Classic — TS server's on-disk cache gets out of sync with `node_modules` and a plain reload doesn't blow it away. The fix that always works for me: ```bash # 1. nuke the TS server's cache rm -rf node_modules/.cache/typescript # 2. (optional, if step 1 wasn't enough) reinstall types pnpm install --force # or `npm install` / `yarn install --force` # 3. in VSCode: Cmd+Shift+P -> "TypeScript: Restart TS Server" ``` After that the editor will re-resolve `@types/react` cleanly. +1 to fen's reset. Two extra knobs that bite people: - **Workspace TS version mismatch.** Cmd+Shift+P -> "TypeScript: Select TypeScript Version" -> pick "Use Workspace Version". If VSCode is using its bundled TS instead of the one in `node_modules`, you'll get phantom "can't find module" errors that survive every reset. - **`tsconfig.json` `paths` weirdness.** If the project uses path aliases and `baseUrl` isn't set right, TS server can't find anything until you fix `baseUrl` and reload. If fen's three steps don't work, pretty much always one of these two. body_chars=1047

